## 6. What Builders Should Look For in Reference Material

When evaluating a repo or guide, look for the following:

### Strong signs
- clear product flow
- clear folder structure
- testable implementation
- documented assumptions
- explicit network configuration
- real transaction handling
- useful build reports or notes

### Weak signs
- outdated SDK usage
- unclear asset assumptions
- no error handling
- no explanation of why the architecture was chosen
- demo-only code with no clarity on how it actually works

Use reference repos to accelerate understanding, not to copy blindly.

